-3cff11531a79.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f37b/72.png\" alt=\"🍻\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span> From the motherland!<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Rothaus Eiszapfle</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Weihenstephaner Festbier</span></span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/a99283a1-32f8-175a-ecb5-47fa92f82ddf.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>👊 Something for erbody<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Jack’s Abby Fest of Both Worlds</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hoppy Pilsner<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Vasen Blueberry Lemonade Otter</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Sour<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Dogfish Head Boy Howdy</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Cream Ale</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/ff3d57ce-b724-2775-5638-6fa0566c4217.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍁 Seasonals for days<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Atlas Festbier</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Smuttynose Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Old Nation Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Sloop Yes Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Ale</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/3f1a017e-1849-aa50-630e-2a533a7b89c0.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🌞 New N/As <br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Athletic Oktoberfest </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Festbier<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Best Day Endless Mango</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> IPA<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Lawson’s Sip'N</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> IPA</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/4db9d684-5e35-df6a-6f46-74c58c3876e8.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f929/72.png\" alt=\"🤩\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> Psyched to see </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Schilling</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Konstantin </span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>Marzen<br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Palmovka</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Czech Pilsner</span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/e0355ac4-2ed1-eb4a-5bf3-a9c6cb0e282c.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f9e1/72.png\" alt=\"🧡\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> It's Fall in VA<br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Bold Rock Honeycrisp </span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>Cider<br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Starr Hill Fall Variety Pack</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> with </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Northern Lights</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> West Coast IPA, </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Festie</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Oktoberfest, </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Last Leaf</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Maple Brown &amp;</span></span></span><strong><span><span><span> Reviver</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Red IPA</span></span></span></p>\n<p>Precarious Omnidirectional Squeegee DIPA</p>\n<p>Outer Range Apres All Day Lager</p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/bb6960f5-015a-d8be-4053-f770e2a0b280.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Vina Nora Peitan Albarino Rias Baixas</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>If Albarino were a person, it would show up to every party in a linen shirt, smelling like the ocean, and somehow make friends with absolutely everyone. Truly, in my past life as a CPA, I once wowed a bunch of partners with a bottle of Albarino. Peitán is the estate's single-vineyard expression, and it shows - lemon, crispy apple, white flowers and the signature saline minerality that reminds you exactly what to pair with that linen shirt: Oysters.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Les Parcellaires de l'Herré Colombard Ugni Blanc</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>Domaine de l'Herré sits at the foot of the Pyrenees on the historic golden sands of Bas Armagnac, which are legendary for producing whites of exceptional aromatic intensity. An aromatic, affordable French white at a breezy 11% ABV? Yes, please. Delightful and easy with tropical fruits, squeezes of fresh citrus and light floral undertones.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span>Gibele Pellegrino</span></span><span><span>: </span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Aromatic white fans, buckle up. Zibibbo isn't just fun to say, it's also fun to drink, and it provides some of the most intense and lively floral notes you're going to find. Capturing Sicily's sun-drenched, sea-swept soul in a bottle with a dry, vivid palate of citrus, yellow peach and green apple. Certified Organic.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/542464a3-e5e6-ffe9-0703-18b1c0725ba6.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Castellano Pinot Grigio</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> is a cute new late summer addition to the shop! Even before working at the shop, I was a hardcore Brew Shop supporter and Wine Club Member. I always looked for key words like crispy, lemon-lime, zesty, (crushable, wink) and of course a cute label. Naturally I was intrigued to try it based on the cute bird decal and super affordable price point of $12.99. This clean and crisp Italian light bodied babe checks all my boxes. It is super easy to pair with light apps, a seafood dish, or watching soccer in bed! Speaking from personal experience, of course.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>This little birdie comes from Veneto, the part of northern Italy that is home to some of the best Pinot Grigio in the world. I got the chance to visit the GORGEOUS canal city of Venice for a short day last summer, and secretly my top highlight was having the best grocery store sandwich of my life in a cute little Piazza near the canals. While I often enjoyed spritzes in Venice, a cold glass of Pinot Grigio never failed to cool me down. You can’t beat those green apple flavors and citrusy tang. The Castellano holds true as a perfectly zippy glass with lots of personality and flavor to keep things interesting.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>As I am writing this write up I sold two bottles! I feel like the Italian winemakers are smiling from their mountainous hilltops. Give her a try, I hope you enjoy it as much as I did!</span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Abby</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/ac2639d9-7c97-6f99-4b16-27bd4f299ef2.jpeg\" width=\"612\" alt=\"breathe11x17in_2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
